THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS UNDER OTHER TERMS
================================================================================

The MIT terms above cover the code written for this project. This repository
also redistributes third-party code, which keeps its own licence. Nothing above
replaces or weakens those terms, and nothing below applies to anything except
the paths it names.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bddisasm 3.0.1 - Apache License 2.0
    libkofemu/bddisasm/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) Bitdefender. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The instruction decoder the emulator is built on. ONE FILE IS MODIFIED:
`src/bdx86_decoder.c` carries a single-condition fix to the 16-bit addressing
displacement guard, marked `KOFENG PATCH` at the site. Every other file is
redistributed unmodified. The full licence text travels with them at
`libkofemu/bddisasm/LICENSE`; the provenance, the exact subset taken and what
the patch fixes are recorded in `libkofemu/bddisasm/README.kofeng.md`.

Apache 2.0 requires that a copy of the licence travel with the code, that
existing copyright and attribution notices are kept, and that modified files
say they were modified. All three are satisfied: by the paths above, and by the
marking at the patch site and in the two READMEs. See THIRD-PARTY.md.

